    "https://tamus.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/job/Commerce-TX/Police-Officer_R-079328": {
      "title": "Police Officer",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-09-02\nPosted: Posted 3 Days Ago\nFull time\n\nJob Title Police Officer Agency East Texas A&M University Department University Police Proposed Minimum Salary Commensurate Job Location Commerce, Texas Job Type Staff Job Description INSTRUCTIONS TO APPLICANT: During the application process the “My Experience ” page has a section provided “ Attachments (Resume/CV, References, Cover letter, etc.) ” to upload required documents.  Use the Upload button to add each document. You will be able to upload up to 5 documents. Be aware that the maximum size allowed for any one document is 5MB. All documents must be electronically submitted through the Texas A&M Online Employment Services website to be considered. Incomplete or improperly submitted applications may be excluded from consideration.  Please provide the following documents: Cover Letter Resume/CV Three professional references with complete contact information (Unsolicited letters of recommendation will not be considered). Transcripts (Unofficial will be accepted with application. Official transcripts are required at time of verbal offer).  If transcripts are from an international institution, it is the responsibility of the applicant to have the transcripts translated and evaluated by an approved credential evaluator. Please do not withdraw your application in an attempt to upload a missing document. If you need assistance with this or any other matter, please contact us at HR.Hiring@etamu.edu . A Presidential proclamation issued on September 19, 2025, imposes a $100,000 fee on new H-1B petitions filed after September 21, 2025. Please be advised that Texas A&M University will NOT pay this fee. Therefore, if you need immigration sponsorship for your employment, we recommend that you consult with your private immigration counsel at your own expense to ascertain whether your current immigration status would make a potential offer of employment from Texas A&M University subject to this fee. In addition, on January 27, 2026, Texas Governor Abbot issued a moratorium on the filing of any new H-1B unless approved by the Texas Workforce Commission. Accordingly, if you will now or in the future require sponsorship for employment visa status this moratorium may affect our ability to employ you should you be selected as the final candidate. Annual Salary of $60,000.00 SUMMARY: The Police Officer, under general supervision, provides specialized professional law enforcement skills by giving service, information, and aid to the university community and campus facilities as circumstances require, preventing crime, suppressing disturbances, investigating criminal offenses, and arresting offenders. DUTIES & RESPONSIBILITIES: Patrols designated areas by vehicle, on foot, or by bicycle to prevent, discover, and deter the commission of crime, to enforce criminal law, to direct traffic, and to enforce motor vehicle operation and parking regulations. Responds to calls and complaints involving the violation(s) of criminal law. Writes detailed reports on police-related activities. Interviews complainants and generates reports to be forwarded to CID or other departments as needed. Secures crime scenes, conducts preliminary and follow-up investigations, gathers evidence, obtains witness statements, apprehends suspects, makes arrests, and transports offenders. Be available to assist faculty, staff and students with general information, inquiries, or other needs. Testifies as a witness in court in connection with arrests, juvenile hearings, depositions, and similar proceedings. Serves arrest warrants, search warrants and other papers, as required. Keeps informed and aware of persons and places suspected of illegal activity and/or the potential for problems within an assigned area. Responsible for decisions as to the appropriate action necessary in accordance with rules, regulations, policies, federal, state, and local laws. Recognizes and reports safety hazards. Develop and maintain required skills and certificates. Attends continuing education courses/law enforcement training. Uses and properly cares for firearms and related police emergency equipment. Must wear and effectively utilize all department issued equipment, as well as, maintain provided uniform and equipment and present a professional appearance and image. Operate a motor vehicle safely while utilizing a police radio and other emergency equipment. Operate and qualify with the department issued firearms, utilizing both hands, as well as with each hand individually. Operate office equipment, camera systems and field equipment. Retain and retrieve information furnished in the form of bulletins, verbal reports, briefings, and training. Project a professional image, both on duty and off, as dictated by Texas A&M-Commerce Police Department policy and procedure. MINIMUM REQUIREMENTS: Education: High school diploma or equivalent AND: Minimum of twelve (12) hours of college credit from an accredited college or university (must provide documentation of college credit with an official transcript) OR Minimum of one (1) year of active duty in any branch of the U.S. Armed Forces. No equivalency will be granted unless the candidate was honorably discharged and has a DD Form 214 to document service and type of discharge. If the candidate is currently serving in the Reserves / Guard and a DD Form 214 is not available, appropriate documentation form the candidate’s unit verifying active duty service will suffice. Experience / Knowledge / Skills Fluent in American English. Proficient in American English grammar and spelling. Strong interpersonal and organizational skills. Ability to: Multitask and work cooperatively with others. Work beyond normal office hours and/or work on weekends and/or holidays. Communicate effectively with all segments of the campus population. Function under adverse and stressful conditions. Licensing/Professional Certifications: Valid driver license and good driving record. Texas Commission on Law Enforcement (TCOLE) license. All system university police will be required to meet minimum licensing standard requirements as required by the Texas Commission on Law Enforcement (TCOLE) § 217.1. Physical/Psychological Requirements: Ability to obtain a passing Texas Commission on Law Enforcement (TCOLE) Licensee Medical Condition Declaration (L-2). Ability to obtain a passing Texas Commission on Law Enforcement (TCOLE) Licensee Psychological and Emotional Health Declaration (L-3). Other Requirements: Background investigation and testing to include psychological examination required.  May be required to submit to polygraph exam and drug testing.  Due to the position you are applying for requires access to CJI systems, if it is found you have any of the following convictions on your criminal history report your application will be disqualified:  Felony Conviction Felony Deferred Adjudication Class A Misdemeanor Conviction Class A Misdemeanor Deferred Adjudication Family Violence Conviction Open arrest for any criminal offense (felony or misdemeanor) will be disqualified until disposition. The following will be a disqualifier for the amount of time listed: Class B Misdemeanor Conviction – 10 years Class B Misdemeanor Deferred Adjudication – 10 years PREFERRED EDUCATION / SKILLS/ EXPERIENCE: Three (3) years of experience as a commissioned law enforcement officer OR the equivalency of one of the following: Minimum of thirty (30) hours of college credit from an accredited college or university (must provide documentation of college credit with an official transcript) OR Minimum of three (3) years of active duty in any branch of the U.S. Armed Forces. No equivalency will be granted unless the candidate was honorably discharged and has a DD Form 214 to document service and type of discharge. If the candidate is currently serving in the Reserves / Guard and a DD Form 214 is not available, appropriate documentation form the candidate’s unit verifying active duty service will suffice. SUPERVISION OF OTHERS: None WHY WORK AT EAST TEXAS A&M UNIVERSITY? Competitive Benefits & Work-Life Balance: Employee tuition assistance   for master’s and doctoral programs. Comprehensive benefits   package including health, dental, vision, life, and long-term disability insurance. ETAMU contributes   to employee health and basic life insurance premiums. 12-15 days of   annual paid holidays , plus up to eight hours of   paid sick leave and vacation   each month. Automatic enrollment in the   Teacher Retirement System of Texas (TRS) ,   with optional additional retirement plans (ORP). Physical wellness program   and wellness release time for eligible employees. Career Growth & Development: Access to cutting-edge research opportunities at a designated   R2 Research Institution . Academic Excellence: ETAMU is ranked among the top   30% in five online degree programs   and offers national recognized academic programs. Over 140 degree programs , including nationally ranked online and graduate options. First accredited institution   to offer a competency-based bachelor’s degree in   criminal justice . Distance education   offerings in Corsicana, Dallas, Frisco, McKinney, Mesquite, Bryan, and online. State-of-the-Art Facilities: Work in advanced facilities such as the   113,470-square-foot Nursing and Health Sciences Building , featuring a state-of-the-art   simulation hospital   and a   1,300-acre agricultural research farm . Vibrant Campus Life: Engage with over   95 student organizations   and   14 NCAA Division I athletic teams , contributing to a thriving campus community. Prime Location & Growth: Enjoy the benefits of working in rapidly growing regions, with abundant career opportunities at   six locations across Dallas and Northeast Texas. Visit us on our social media: Facebook ,   Twitter ,   Instagram ,   YouTube ,   LinkedIn ,   and   ETAMU News All positions are security-sensitive. Applicants are subject to a criminal history investigation, and employment is contingent upon the institution’s verification of credentials and/or other information required by the institution’s procedures, including the completion of the criminal history check. Equal Opportunity/Veterans/Disability Employer."
    },
    "https://tamus.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/job/Commerce-TX/Open-Rank-Professor---Educational-Leadership_R-096667-1": {
      "title": "Open Rank-Professor - Educational Leadership",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-08-31\nPosted: Posted 5 Days Ago\nFull time\n\nJob Title Open Rank-Professor - Educational Leadership Agency East Texas A&M University Department Educational Leadership Proposed Minimum Salary Commensurate Job Location Commerce, Texas Job Type Faculty Job Description INSTRUCTIONS TO APPLICANT : During the application process the “My Experience ” page has a section provided “ Attachments (Resume/CV, References, Cover letter, etc.) ” to upload required documents.  Use the Upload button to add each document. You will be able to upload up to 5 documents. Be aware that the maximum size allowed for any one document is 5MB. All documents must be electronically submitted through the Texas A&M Online Employment Services website to be considered. Incomplete or improperly submitted applications may be excluded from consideration. Please do not withdraw your application in an attempt to upload a missing document, instead please email HR for help. Please provide the following documents : Cover Letter Resume/CV Three professional references with complete contact information (Unsolicited letters of recommendation will not be considered). Transcripts (Unofficial will be accepted with application. Official transcripts are required upon acceptance of verbal offer).  If transcripts are from an international institution, it is the responsibility of the prospective faculty member to have the transcripts translated and evaluated by an approved credential evaluator. If you need assistance, please contact us at HR.Hiring@etamu.edu A Presidential proclamation issued on September 19, 2025, imposes a $100,000 fee on new H-1B petitions filed after September 21, 2025. Please be advised that Texas A&M University will NOT pay this fee. Therefore, if you need immigration sponsorship for your employment, we recommend that you consult with your private immigration counsel at your own expense to ascertain whether your current immigration status would make a potential offer of employment from Texas A&M University subject to this fee. In addition, on January 27, 2026, Texas Governor Abbot issued a moratorium on the filing of any new H-1B unless approved by the Texas Workforce Commission. Accordingly, if you will now or in the future require sponsorship for employment visa status this moratorium may affect our ability to employ you should you be selected as the final candidate. SUMMARY: The Department of Educational Leadership is seeking to fill one tenure-track, open-rank faculty position with a nine-month academic appointment beginning in Spring 2027. Faculty are expected to maintain an active record of scholarly and professional engagement, collaborate effectively with others, and contribute meaningful service to the discipline, the university, and the broader community. As a proud member of the third-largest institution in The Texas A&M University System, ETAMU fosters a strong professional environment that supports career growth and academic excellence. ETAMU is a fast-growing public university with a strong reputation for academic excellence, research innovation, and student success. With over 140+ degree programs, a 20:1 student-to-faculty ratio, and nationally ranked online and graduate programs, ETAMU is committed to transforming lives through quality education. Our employees benefit from a collaborative community, cutting-edge research opportunities, and outstanding resources. DUTIES & RESPONSIBILITIES: Teach master’s and doctoral level courses in educational leadership; Design, conduct, and publish research to include publications in peer-reviewed journals Advise students; Prepare syllabi; Update course materials; Develop curriculum; Deliver instruction both online and face-to-face at any of the university’s sites; instructional duties may include teaching during the day, the evening, or Saturday; Work collaboratively with faculty and staff to implement departmental programs; Provide service to the department, college, university, public schools, and the community; Maintain knowledge and stay abreast of current trends in learning via research, best practices, and technological applications in the classroom that include online instruction; and Chair dissertations to completion. MINIMUM REQUIREMENTS: Education: doctorate in educational leadership or educational administration from a regionally- accredited U.S. university Experience/Knowledge/Skills: 3 years of K-12 teaching experience. 3 years of experience as a public-school administrator. Experience teaching online in higher education. Strong interpersonal skills and the ability to work collaboratively with a team of professionals; strong written and oral communication skills; commitment to high quality instruction; dedication to high standards and student success; record of or potential for scholarship; strong quantitative and qualitative analysis skills Ability to: multitask and work collegially as part of a team Licensing/Professional Certifications: principal certification Physical Requirements: not applicable PREFERRED EDUCATION/SKILL/EXPERIENCE : Experience teaching in a graduate program Experience chairing dissertations to completion Superintendent Certification and Experience Record of publication All positions are security-sensitive. Applicants are subject to a criminal history investigation, and employment is contingent upon the institution’s verification of credentials and/or other information required by the institution’s procedures, including the completion of the criminal history check. Equal Opportunity/Veterans/Disability Employer."
    },
    "https://tamus.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/job/Commerce-TX/Assistant-Director-of-Communications-and-Media-Relations_R-096693-2": {
      "title": "Assistant Director of Communications and Media Relations",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-08-31\nPosted: Posted 5 Days Ago\nFull time\n\nJob Title Assistant Director of Communications and Media Relations Agency East Texas A&M University Department Marketing Communications Proposed Minimum Salary Commensurate Job Location Commerce, Texas Job Type Staff Job Description INSTRUCTIONS TO APPLICANT: During the application process the “My Experience ” page has a section provided “ Attachments (Resume/CV, References, Cover letter, etc.) ” to upload required documents.  Use the Upload button to add each document. You will be able to upload up to 5 documents. Be aware that the maximum size allowed for any one document is 5MB. All documents must be electronically submitted through the Texas A&M Online Employment Services website to be considered. Incomplete or improperly submitted applications may be excluded from consideration. Please do not withdraw your application in an attempt to upload a missing document, instead please email HR for help. Please provide the following documents : Cover Letter Resume/CV Three professional references with complete contact information (Unsolicited letters of recommendation will not be considered). Transcripts (Unofficial will be accepted with application. Official transcripts are required upon acceptance of verbal offer).  If transcripts are from an international institution, it is the responsibility of the prospective faculty member to have the transcripts translated and evaluated by an approved credential evaluator. If you need assistance, please contact us at HR.Hiring@tamuc.edu A Presidential proclamation issued on September 19, 2025, imposes a $100,000 fee on new H-1B petitions filed after September 21, 2025. Please be advised that Texas A&M University will NOT pay this fee. Therefore, if you need immigration sponsorship for your employment, we recommend that you consult with your private immigration counsel at your own expense to ascertain whether your current immigration status would make a potential offer of employment from Texas A&M University subject to this fee. In addition, on January 27, 2026, Texas Governor Abbot issued a moratorium on the filing of any new H-1B unless approved by the Texas Workforce Commission. Accordingly, if you will now or in the future require sponsorship for employment visa status this moratorium may affect our ability to employ you should you be selected as the final candidate. SUMMARY: The Assistant Director of Communications and Media Relations leads the planning, management and day-to-day operations of East Texas A&M University’s communications function in support of institutional strategy and priorities established by the Chief Marketing Officer. The position develops communications plans, establishes project workflows, manages staff and resources, works directly with university stakeholders, and leads the editorial planning and institutional storytelling approach across communications functions. The Assistant Director is responsible for moving the communications unit toward established strategic objectives through coordinated planning, execution, measurement, reporting and continuous improvement. The position oversees media relations, university news and owned media, internal communications, e-communications, crisis and issues communications, and the professional staff responsible for those functions. The Assistant Director also collaborates closely with other Marketing and Communications teams to ensure communications efforts are coordinated across channels and contribute to broader university priorities. DUTIES & RESPONSIBILITIES: Communications Leadership, Planning and Operations Leads the planning, management and day-to-day operations of the university communications function. Translates institutional priorities and communications strategy established by the Chief Marketing Officer into actionable plans, workstreams, assignments and timelines. Develops and maintains communications plans, editorial calendars, project workflows, standards and processes that support efficient and coordinated execution. Works directly with university leaders, colleges, divisions and other campus stakeholders to understand communications needs, clarify objectives, establish priorities and determine appropriate communications support. Leads the university’s editorial planning and institutional storytelling arc across communications functions, ensuring planned editorial, responsive news and communications activities reinforce institutional priorities. Assigns work, manages team capacity and staffing, establishes priorities and ensures projects move efficiently from planning through execution. Monitors progress, results and resource needs and provides regular reporting and recommendations to the Chief Marketing Officer. Uses communications performance, audience insights, stakeholder feedback and operational data to improve plans, workflows and allocation of resources. Leads through empowerment, support and shared achievement by providing staff with clear objectives, appropriate authority, context and resources to succeed. Media Relations Supervises the university’s media relations function and the Senior Media Relations Specialist. Provides direction and priorities for proactive earned-media efforts, media pitching, faculty-expert placement, external media relationships and response to media inquiries. Ensures media relations efforts support university priorities, institutional reputation and broader editorial and storytelling objectives. Editorial, University News and Owned Media Leads the university’s editorial plan and storytelling strategy across university news and other owned communications channels. Oversees planned editorial content, responsive and opportunity-driven news, institutional announcements, feature storytelling and other centrally produced university content. Establishes editorial priorities and ensures stories are developed and distributed through the channels and formats most appropriate to the audience and objective. Maintains standards for writing, editing, accuracy, institutional voice and editorial quality across university communications. Oversees the university’s owned media channels within the communications function and ensures they work together as a coordinated system rather than as independent outlets. Maintains the university’s communications lexicon, editorial conventions and related writing standards. Internal Communications Oversees the university’s internal communications function and the staff responsible for faculty and staff communications. Leads planning for faculty and staff communications, including university announcements, leadership messages, digital publications, newsletters and operational information. Ensures internal communications are coordinated, timely and aligned with institutional priorities. Provides communications support to university leaders and campus partners for significant internal initiatives, organizational changes and other institutional needs. E-Communications Oversees the university’s e-communications function and the professional staff responsible for digital communications support. Ensures e-communications services effectively support university priorities and the communications needs of partner areas, including Enrollment Management and Philanthropy and Engagement. Establishes priorities, standards and workflows for email and other digital communications supported by the communications team. Coordinates e-communications activity with broader editorial, internal communications and institutional messaging plans. Crisis and Issues Communications Leads the development, maintenance and regular review of crisis communications plans, protocols and messaging resources for university emergencies, emerging issues and sensitive situations. Coordinates communications execution during crises and emerging issues in collaboration with the Chief Marketing Officer and university leadership. Serves as the primary point of contact for media relations during crises, emerging issues and sensitive situations, coordinating inquiries, responses and information flow as appropriate. Monitors emerging issues and recommends communications approaches, messaging, timing and response needs. Cross-Department Collaboration Collaborates closely with Web, Content, Creative, Design, Social Media, Brand, Marketing and Analytics teams to ensure communications activity is coordinated across the department. Works with cross-functional teams to align storytelling, messaging, content development, audience strategy and distribution across earned, owned, social and digital channels. Participates in integrated planning for major university initiatives, campaigns and institutional priorities. Helps ensure communications plans can be effectively supported and reinforced across the university’s broader marketing and digital ecosystem. Supervision Supervises professional staff responsible for media relations, editorial and storytelling, internal communications and e-communications. Assigns and reviews work, establishes priorities and performance expectations, provides coaching and professional development, and completes performance evaluations. Builds a collaborative team environment centered on empowerment, support, accountability and shared achievement. Encourages professional staff to exercise expertise and sound judgment within established priorities and standards. Performs other duties as assigned. MINIMUM REQUIREMENTS: Education and Experience: Bachelor’s degree in communications, journalism, public relations, English, marketing or a related field, or an equivalent combination of education and experience. Seven years of progressively responsible experience in communications, journalism, media relations, public relations, editorial operations or a related field. Demonstrated experience developing and implementing communications plans. Demonstrated experience in writing, editing, media relations, editorial planning or institutional communications. Experience supervising professional staff or providing significant team leadership. Experience managing multiple projects, priorities and stakeholders in a complex organization. Knowledge/Skills/Abilities: Exceptional writing, editing, verbal communication and interpersonal skills. Strong news judgment and knowledge of journalistic standards, media practices and AP style. Ability to translate strategic objectives into coordinated communications plans and operational priorities. Strong leadership, project management, organizational and staff-management skills. Ability to manage competing priorities, allocate team capacity and maintain effective workflows. Ability to build productive relationships with university leaders, faculty, staff, students, journalists and community partners. Ability to lead editorial planning and identify compelling institutional stories and communications opportunities. Ability to use data, analytics and communications results to evaluate performance and improve future work. Ability to exercise sound judgment, discretion and professionalism during sensitive or rapidly changing situations. Ability to work collaboratively across functional areas and influence outcomes in a complex organization. Ability to work outside regular business hours when emergencies, major announcements or media activity require. Licensing/Professional Certifications: None Physical Requirements: None Other Requirements: This position may require occasional work beyond normal business hours as work requirements indicate. This position must be able to work with confidential or sensitive information and exercise sound judgment in its handling. This position may require occasional travel to other locations and instructional sites. This position’s primary duty station is located in Commerce, TX but may require weekly work at the Dallas educational site. PREFERRED EDUCATION/ SKILLS/EXPERIENCE: Master’s degree in communications, journalism, public relations, marketing or a related field. Communications experience in higher education, government or another complex public organization. Experience leading an institutional communications, editorial or news operation. Experience with earned media, crisis communications and organizational-change communications. Experience advising leaders and working across multiple organizational units. Familiarity with the Texas media environment and public higher education. SUPERVISION OF OTHERS: Responsible for hiring, training and supervising student workers, graduate assistants, staff and support staff CRITICAL INFRASTRUCTURE COMPETENCY: Ability to maintain the security and integrity of critical infrastructure, which may include communications systems, computer networks and systems, cybersecurity systems, electrical grid, hazardous waste treatment system or water treatment system. WHY WORK AT EAST TEXAS A&M UNIVERSITY? Competitive Benefits & Work-Life Balance: Employee tuition assistance for master’s and doctoral programs. Comprehensive benefits package including health, dental, vision, life, and long-term disability insurance. ETAMU contributes to employee health and basic life insurance premiums. 12-15 days of annual paid holidays , plus up to eight hours of paid sick leave and vacation each month. Automatic enrollment in the Teacher Retirement System of Texas (TRS) , with optional additional retirement plans (ORP). Physical wellness program and wellness release time for eligible employees. Career Growth & Development: Access to cutting-edge research opportunities at a designated R2 Research Institution . Academic Excellence: ETAMU is ranked among the top 30% in five online degree programs and offers national recognized academic programs. Over 140 degree programs , including nationally ranked online and graduate options. First accredited institution to offer a competency-based bachelor’s degree in criminal justice . Distance education offerings in Corsicana, Dallas, Frisco, McKinney, Mesquite, Bryan, and online. State-of-the-Art Facilities: Work in advanced facilities such as the 113,470-square-foot Nursing and Health Sciences Building , featuring a state-of-the-art simulation hospital and a 1,300-acre agricultural research farm . Vibrant Campus Life: Engage with over 95 student organizations and 14 NCAA Division I athletic teams , contributing to a thriving campus community. Prime Location & Growth: Enjoy the benefits of working in rapidly growing regions, with abundant career opportunities at six locations across Dallas and Northeast Texas. Visit us on our social media: Facebook , Twitter , Instagram , YouTube , LinkedIn , and ETAMU News All positions are security-sensitive. Applicants are subject to a criminal history investigation, and employment is contingent upon the institution’s verification of credentials and/or other information required by the institution’s procedures, including the completion of the criminal history check. Equal Opportunity/Veterans/Disability Employer."
    },
