articipation, performance in class, assignments, and examinations. Assist/mentor students as needed. Attend online paralegal program faculty meetings. Other duties as assigned. MINIMUM REQUIREMENTS: Education: Juris Doctorate. Experience: Three years of experience practicing law.  Must have previous experience working with paralegals/legal assistants.  Knowledge / Skills:   Must be knowledgeable and remain current in the subject matter of assigned courses.  Demonstrate excellent oral and written communication skills to facilitate instruction in classes and engagement with students.  Ability to: Multi-task and work cooperatively with others.  Have the ability to learn online platforms and conduct virtual meetings with students. Licensing/Professional Certifications: Licensed by a state bar. Physical Requirements: XYZ Other Requirements: XYZ PREFERRED EDUCATION / SKILLS/ EXPERIENCE: Prior College or University teaching experience or other teaching experience related to the legal field. Evidence of teaching excellence. Online or hybrid teaching experience. SUPERVISION OF OTHERS: N/A All positions are security-sensitive. Applicants are subject to a criminal history investigation, and employment is contingent upon the institution’s verification of credentials and/or other information required by the institution’s procedures, including the completion of the criminal history check. Equal Opportunity/Veterans/Disability Employer."
