    "https://tamus.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/job/Commerce-TX/Quail-Research-Laboratory-Manager_R-094185-1": {
      "title": "Quail Research Laboratory Manager",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-06-15\nPosted: Posted 30+ Days Ago\nFull time\n\nJob Title Quail Research Laboratory Manager Agency East Texas A&M University Department President's Office Proposed Minimum Salary Commensurate Job Location Commerce, Texas Job Type Staff Job Description INSTRUCTIONS TO APPLICANT: During the application process the “My Experience ” page has a section provided “ Attachments (Resume/CV, References, Cover letter, etc.) ” to upload required documents.  Use the Upload button to add each document. You will be able to upload up to 5 documents. Be aware that the maximum size allowed for any one document is 5MB. All documents must be electronically submitted through the Texas A&M Online Employment Services website to be considered. Incomplete or improperly submitted applications may be excluded from consideration. Please do not withdraw your application in an attempt to upload a missing document, instead please email HR for help. Please provide the following documents : Cover Letter Resume/CV Three professional references with complete contact information (Unsolicited letters of recommendation will not be considered). Transcripts (Unofficial will be accepted with application. Official transcripts are required upon acceptance of verbal offer).  If transcripts are from an international institution, it is the responsibility of the prospective faculty member to have the transcripts translated and evaluated by an approved credential evaluator. If you need assistance, please contact us at HR.Hiring@tamuc.edu A Presidential proclamation issued on September 19, 2025, imposes a $100,000 fee on new H-1B petitions filed after September 21, 2025. Please be advised that Texas A&M University will NOT pay this fee. Therefore, if you need immigration sponsorship for your employment, we recommend that you consult with your private immigration counsel at your own expense to ascertain whether your current immigration status would make a potential offer of employment from Texas A&M University subject to this fee. In addition, on January 27, 2026, Texas Governor Abbot issued a moratorium on the filing of any new H-1B unless approved by the Texas Workforce Commission. Accordingly, if you will now or in the future require sponsorship for employment visa status this moratorium may affect our ability to employ you should you be selected as the final candidate. SUMMARY: The Ted and Donna Lyon Center for Gamebird Research at East Texas A&M University is a cutting-edge research facility with a mission to discover solutions for sustainable gamebird populations, train the next generation of gamebird professionals, and transform the gamebird industry. The Lyon Center is recruiting a highly motivated and experienced research laboratory manager to oversee the daily operation of The Reyna Laboratory for Upland Gamebirds, while promoting the center’s mission. The lab manager will play a critical role in supporting research by ensuring the laboratory facilities operate efficiently, safely, and in compliance with university, state, and federal regulations. The successful candidate will be responsible for managing the day-to-day operation of the research laboratory, including developing and implementing research projects, supervising staff, and adhering to animal use and safety protocols. This position is ideal for an individual with experience in research, excellent management skills, and a commitment to foster a collaborative and innovative workplace. Candidates should have experience in managing a research laboratory, with preference given to candidates with experience working in a quail/upland gamebird/avian laboratory and with knowledge of quail/upland gamebirds/avian research and conservation. The director of the Lyon Center will work closely with the selected candidate to provide ample professional development. DUTIES & RESPONSIBILITIES: Supervise, train, and mentor lab technicians Ensure adherence to safety regulations and protocols Maintain a safe working environment and conduct regular inspections. Oversee the operation, maintenance, calibration, and repair of laboratory equipment. Implement and maintain quality control measures to ensure accurate and reliable results. Manage inventory, order supplies, and ensure a sufficient supply of materials for experiments. Perform administrative duties such as project management, scheduling, record-keeping, and reporting. Provide technical support for research experiments, coordinate research projects, and assist in data analysis. Acting as a liaison between the lab and other departments, researchers, and clients. Participate in programmatic and strategic planning for the Reyna Lab and Lyon Center Supporting the Lyon Center and its mission MINIMUM REQUIREMENTS: Education and Experience: Bachelor’s degree in biology or related field. 2+ years of related professional experience in the laboratory environment, including experience in a leadership or supervisory role. Experience working in a quail/upland gamebird/avian research laboratory is preferred. The ideal candidate has a passion for upland gamebird research. Knowledge / Skills: Demonstrated excellent verbal and written communication skills. Knowledge and experience with laboratory equipment, procedures, and relevant analytical techniques (e.g., HPLC, ELISA). Knowledge of management and supervision principles, including staffing, performance evaluation, and training. Project management. Ability to: manage multiple priorities, organize workflows, work effectively, communicate technical information effectively, establish positive working relationships, resolve conflicts , operate within a budget, identify problems and recommend solutions, ensure compliance, and represent the Lyon Center with professionalism. Licensing/Professional Certifications: N/A Physical Requirements: Ability to walk, stand, bend, and lift for extended periods, ability to lift 30 lbs., be outdoors for extended periods, ability to communicate for the duration of shifts or events. Other Requirements: May be required to work weekends or work hours outside of a normal schedule. Possible exposure to dust, animal dander, heat/humidity, direct sunlight, animal byproducts (including mortality), precipitation, and mud. PREFERRED EDUCATION / SKILLS/ EXPERIENCE: The ideal candidate: Has experience managing a quail/upland gamebird/avian research laboratory, producing research results, and supervising staff. Demonstrates proficiency in laboratory safety and biosecurity. Demonstrates impeccable organizational, project management, and time management skills. Is detail-oriented with the ability to meet deadlines. Understands the importance of upland gamebird research. Prioritizes the mission of the Reyna Laboratory and the Lyon Center for Gamebird Research. Exudes professionalism. Has experience working in a higher education setting or familiarity with university processes, or working with research, conservation, or non-profit organizations. Enjoys interacting with the public, donors, public agencies, and corporate and non-profit partners. Has a passion and understanding for gamebirds, conservation, and/or the outdoors. CRITICAL INFRASTRUCTURE COMPETENCY: Ability to maintain the security and integrity of critical infrastructure, which may include communications systems, computer networks and systems, cybersecurity systems, electrical grid, hazardous waste treatment system or water treatment system. WHY WORK AT EAST TEXAS A&M UNIVERSITY? Competitive Benefits & Work-Life Balance: Employee tuition assistance for master’s and doctoral programs. Comprehensive benefits package including health, dental, vision, life, and long-term disability insurance. ETAMU contributes to employee health and basic life insurance premiums. 12-15 days of annual paid holidays , plus up to eight hours of paid sick leave and vacation each month. Automatic enrollment in the Teacher Retirement System of Texas (TRS) , with optional additional retirement plans (ORP). Physical wellness program and wellness release time for eligible employees. Career Growth & Development: Access to cutting-edge research opportunities at a designated R2 Research Institution . Academic Excellence: ETAMU is ranked among the top 30% in five online degree programs and offers national recognized academic programs. Over 140 degree programs , including nationally ranked online and graduate options. First accredited institution to offer a competency-based bachelor’s degree in criminal justice . Distance education offerings in Corsicana, Dallas, Frisco, McKinney, Mesquite, Bryan, and online. State-of-the-Art Facilities: Work in advanced facilities such as the 113,470-square-foot Nursing and Health Sciences Building , featuring a state-of-the-art simulation hospital and a 1,300-acre agricultural research farm . Vibrant Campus Life: Engage with over 95 student organizations and 14 NCAA Division I athletic teams , contributing to a thriving campus community. Prime Location & Growth: Enjoy the benefits of working in rapidly growing regions, with abundant career opportunities at six locations across Dallas and Northeast Texas. Visit us on our social media: Facebook , Twitter , Instagram , YouTube , LinkedIn , and ETAMU News All positions are security-sensitive. Applicants are subject to a criminal history investigation, and employment is contingent upon the institution’s verification of credentials and/or other information required by the institution’s procedures, including the completion of the criminal history check. Equal Opportunity/Veterans/Disability Employer."
    },
